---
import SiteHeader from '../components/layout/SiteHeader';
import Container from '../components/layout/Container';
import Section from '../components/layout/Section';
import TipBox from '../components/layout/TipBox';
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/components.css';

// Article metadata (from article.md frontmatter)
const metadata = {
  title: "What the Hell is Deadlock's Midgame?",
  subtitle:
    "A complete beginner's guide to surviving the transition from lane phase to MOBA-style macro gameplay",
  status: 'draft', // draft | review | published
  videoUrl: 'https://youtu.be/k9R1xNCqJ5Y',
  videoId: 'k9R1xNCqJ5Y',
  channel: 'BigBenDL',
  publishDate: '2024-10-08', // Fixed year from article.md
  duration: '12:03',
  readTime: '8 min read',
};

// Check if page should be visible (hide drafts in production)
const isDraft = metadata.status === 'draft';
const isReview = metadata.status === 'review';
const isProduction = import.meta.env.PROD;

// Hide draft pages in production
if (isDraft && isProduction) {
  return Astro.redirect('/guides');
}
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <title>{metadata.title} - Deadlock Fight Club</title>
    <meta name="description" content={metadata.subtitle} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={`${metadata.title} - Deadlock Fight Club`} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={metadata.subtitle} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader client:load />
    <main>
      <Container maxWidth="md">
        <!-- Draft/Review Banner -->
        {
          (isDraft || isReview) && (
            <div
              style={`
            background: ${isDraft ? 'rgba(255, 140, 66, 0.1)' : 'rgba(124, 77, 255, 0.1)'};
            border: 2px solid ${isDraft ? 'var(--accent-orange)' : 'var(--accent-purple)'};
            border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);
            padding: var(--spacing-md);
            margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
            text-align: center;
          `}
            >
              <strong
                style={`color: ${isDraft ? 'var(--accent-orange)' : 'var(--accent-purple)'};`}
              >
                {isDraft ? '🚧 DRAFT MODE' : '📝 UNDER REVIEW'}
              </strong>
              <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);">
                {isDraft
                  ? 'This page is in draft mode and hidden in production builds.'
                  : 'This page is under review. Look for 📝 markers for review comments.'}
              </p>
            </div>
          )
        }

        <!-- Header -->
        <Section>
          <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);">
            <h1
              style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent-orange) 0%, var(--accent-purple) 100%); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; background-clip: text; margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);"
            >
              {metadata.title}
            </h1>
            <p
              style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto var(--spacing-md);"
            >
              {metadata.subtitle}
            </p>
            <div
              style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: var(--spacing-md); flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);"
            >
              <span>By {metadata.channel}</span>
              <span>•</span>
              <span>{metadata.readTime}</span>
              <span>•</span>
              <a
                href={metadata.videoUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); text-decoration: none;"
              >
                🎥 Watch Original Video
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- TL;DR / Overview -->
          <TipBox title="📖 Guide Overview" variant="info">
            <p>
              If you've played Deadlock for even a couple of hours, that moment has come to you.
              You're in lane phase, things are making sense. You trade kills, you push creeps, and
              you try to get that tower at the end. Then, suddenly, some towers start to fall,
              objectives appear all around the map, and the team scatters out of your lane.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              <strong>Deadlock is sneaky.</strong> It's a hero shooter with some extra rules. But once
              towers fall, Deadlock reveals its true identity: <strong
                >It's a MOBA wearing a hero shooter's jacket.</strong
              >
            </p>
            <p
              style="margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);"
            >
              <strong>⚡ TL;DR?</strong> Jump to the <a
                href="#quick-reference"
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); text-decoration: underline;">Quick Reference</a
              > for the 6 core principles you need to master.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
              <strong>Read time:</strong> Full guide is {metadata.readTime} • Quick Reference is 2 min
            </p>
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Wave Management and Macro -->
        <Section id="wave-management" title="🌊 Wave Management and Macro">
          <p>
            Here's the thing: <strong>ignoring wave is the fastest way to lose the game.</strong>
            As people chase kills in the jungle and fights over urn, walkers fall while nobody's looking.
            And regardless of rank, bad macro is bad gameplay. It isn't the most glamorous job, but somebody's
            gotta do it.
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-orange); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              What is Macro?
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              <strong>It's everything beyond the immediate duel.</strong> It's how our objectives are
              standing, how our lanes are pushed, and how our rotations are done on time to ensure that
              those walkers don't take some extra creep damage.
            </p>
            <p
              style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-style: italic;"
            >
              "Macro is also communicating when you can't cover lane. If you see creeps crashing
              your side lane walker while you're on the other side in the middle of the jungle, call
              it out."
            </p>
          </div>

          <TipBox variant="success" title="💡 Pro Tip" style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);">
            The lower your rank, the more likely it is that your teammates are suffering from tunnel
            vision and ignoring the vital objective. Be the one who calls it out.
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Walker Stats -->
        <Section id="walkers" title="🏰 Walker Stats and Why They Matter">
          <p>
            We've been talking about objectives and walkers, but what the hell are they? Here are
            some walker stats to help you know exactly why they're so important:
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-md);"
          >
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
            >
              <div style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700;">
                5,800 HP
              </div>
              <div style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);">
                Side Lane Walkers
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
            >
              <div style="color: var(--accent-purple); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700;">
                9,000+ HP
              </div>
              <div style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);">
                Blue Lane Walker
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
            >
              <div style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700;">15%</div>
              <div style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);">
                Spirit & Bullet Resist Aura
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-orange); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              Why Do Walkers Matter?
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              <strong>Because they change the economy of the entire game.</strong>
            </p>
            <ul style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); padding-left: 1.5rem;">
              <li>One walker down = one extra item slot</li>
              <li>Three walkers down = two extra item slots</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);">
              This is both an economic and power advantage over the opposing team and can ensure
              that the next fight you take is one where your team is heavily bolstered in
              comparison.
            </p>
          </div>

          <TipBox
            variant="warning"
            title="⚠️ Critical Timing"
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);"
          >
            <strong>Wasting time poking walkers pre-minute 16 is bait.</strong> The walker resistances
            are too high at this point, and your team starts to bleed tempo. The real move is to shove
            the wave, steal their jungle, and wait for that more opportune time to strike.
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- 5-Minute Combat Cycle -->
        <Section id="combat-cycle" title="⏱️ The 5-Minute Combat Cycle">
          <p>
            Every <strong>5 minutes</strong> in Deadlock, urn and bridge buffs respawn. Think of these
            like timers in your head, the metronome of mid game. Teams naturally gravitate to these spawns,
            more so bridge buffs than urn. However, they are the catalyst for many a team fight.
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-purple); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              It's Not About Taking Objectives—It's About Timing
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              The key in these objective and win mechanics is not simply just taking them when they
              spawn, but rather <strong>taking them at the most opportune time.</strong> If you treat
              every 5-minute mark as a checkpoint in the game, it more easily organizes your play.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-orange); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              The Optimal Cycle
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              Between minutes <strong>10 and 14:30</strong>, you should really be farming and trying
              to get your next power spike. Then, as soon as that bridge buff comes online or that
              urn finally drops with your newly acquired item, you can take that fight.
            </p>
            <p
              style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md); padding: var(--spacing-md); background: rgba(255, 140, 66, 0.1); border-radius: var(--border-radius); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);"
            >
              <strong>⚠️ The worst thing you can do:</strong> Still scrambling for camps and boxes and
              sitting on over 2,000 in souls. This is where so many teams lose: they show up late to
              the fight without their power spike and are surprised when they get rolled.
            </p>
          </div>

          <TipBox variant="success" title="💡 Remember" style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);">
            <strong>The urn doesn't win you the fight, the preparation does.</strong> The urn is merely
            the catalyst to get it going.
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Power Spikes -->
        <Section id="power-spikes" title="⚡ Power Spikes and Power Ramping">
          <p>
            Let's dig into that preparation and learn some new terms: <strong>power ramping</strong>
            and
            <strong>power spikes.</strong>
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-orange); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              What is a Power Spike?
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              A power spike is when your character goes from "eh" to "oh god, kill it now." It can
              be an item like Tesla Bullets for Wraith or Ivy, or maybe even an upgraded ability
              like tier 3 on Kelvin's Ice Beam.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);">
              The key is there are points in the game where you yourself are markedly stronger than
              you were before. And in relation to the rest of the lobby, you probably have a higher
              total power cap than others at that exact moment.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-purple); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              Spikes Don't Last Forever
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              However, these spikes don't last forever. Using Tesla Bullets or hitting that tier 3
              is very nice and can get you through that next fight. However, relying on it for more
              than
              <strong>2 or 3 minutes</strong> can seriously start to see some diminishing returns.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); color: var(--accent-orange);">
              <strong>Those couple minutes in between are your window</strong>, and are exactly when
              you should be taking either those urn fights or pushing an objective. If you simply
              wait on it, your spike is wasted.
            </p>
          </div>

          <TipBox variant="info" title="🎯 Syncing Spikes" style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);">
            Power spikes with that 5-minute combat cycle is so essential. If you and 2 or 3 other of
            your teammates all have just bought and are ready for a fight along with the urn
            dropping, then you and your team are cooking up something sweet.
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Farm Priority -->
        <Section id="farm-priority" title="🌾 Farm Priority and Soul Denial">
          <p>
            With all this talk of power spikes and power ramping, it begs the question: how do I hit
            my spikes on time? <strong>Farming.</strong>
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-orange); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-md);">
              Farm Priority Hierarchy
            </h3>
            <ol
              style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--spacing-sm);"
            >
              <li>
                <strong style="color: var(--accent-orange);">Center sacrifices</strong> - Should be focused
                above all, primarily due to the buffs they can give you at a jackpot hit. This will give
                you
                <strong>4 boons</strong> that you typically get from a golden statue and is a fantastic
                way to continually ramp your passive stats.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong style="color: var(--accent-purple);">Jungle creeps</strong> - After center sacrifices,
                we move on to jungle creeps.
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);">
            Think of this as your farm hierarchy. When you're pushing the wave and get it up to
            walker, instead of poking that walker at those early minutes, rotate into their jungle
            and start to steal their resources.
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: rgba(124, 77, 255, 0.1); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-purple); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              Macro Soul Denial
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              This is <strong>macro soul denial.</strong> In lane phase, you can deny by shooting the
              little soul that comes out of the creep. In mid game, you can deny by choking out entire
              soul camps.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);">
              This creates a widened differential between their total possible soul allocation as
              well as your total possible soul allocation. If your team farms efficiently and
              invades smartly, this leads to quicker buys and better buys for that next urn, bridge
              buff, or mid boss fight.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); color: var(--accent-orange);">
              <strong>And the beauty of this denial is that it snowballs.</strong> The more you and your
              team are able to smartly steal, the larger the differential gets, the harder it will be
              for them to push you out of their own jungle.
            </p>
          </div>

          <TipBox
            variant="warning"
            title="⚠️ Always Ask Yourself"
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);"
          >
            Whenever you're not fighting or rotating, ask yourself: <strong
              >what's the highest value farm I could be taking right now?</strong
            > If the answer is boxes in your own jungle, well, you're probably leaving a whole lot of
            soul on the table.
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Map Awareness -->
        <Section id="map-awareness" title="🗺️ Map Awareness and Intuition">
          <p>
            Because the map is free info. You can see where enemies are, primarily <strong
              >where they aren't</strong
            >, and if a wave is pushing too far into one of your lanes. And from all this info, you
            start to predict and intuit what the next move might be.
          </p>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-md);"
          >
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border: 2px solid rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.3);"
            >
              <div style="color: #4caf50; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);">
                ✅ Safe Push Scenario
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                You're in far left lane. You see 3-4 enemies on the mid and right side of map.
                <strong>You can safely shove the lane</strong> due to heavy allocation of enemy team
                members on the other side.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border: 2px solid rgba(244, 67, 54, 0.3);"
            >
              <div style="color: #f44336; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);">
                ❌ Danger Zone
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                <strong
                  >If you see no one on the enemy team, this is a much more dangerous state to be
                  in.</strong
                >
                Pushing the lane is more than likely going to result in you getting ganked.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <h3 style="color: var(--accent-purple); margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);">
              Building Intuition: Pattern Recognition
            </h3>
            <p style="margin: 0;">
              <strong>Intuition is simply practiced pattern recognition.</strong> And the only way to
              build up that, well, play more games.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm);">
              The more you watch the map and the more you start playing, the more you'll be able to
              predict what the enemy team is likely concocting:
            </p>
            <ul style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); padding-left: 1.5rem;">
              <li>What's their win condition right now?</li>
              <li>Where do they need to be in order to get the best advantage?</li>
              <li>What are possibly their next buys?</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <TipBox variant="success" title="💡 Key Insight" style="margin-top: var(--spacing-md);">
            Take all of this info and let it affect your gameplay, trying to <strong
              >counter buy, counter rotate, and even counter push.</strong
            > That's the thought process that turns raw awareness into anticipation and perfect execution.
            <p
              style="margin-top: var(--spacing-sm); color: var(--accent-orange); font-size: 1.1rem;"
            >
              <strong>Deadlock rewards the predictors, not the reactors.</strong>
            </p>
          </TipBox>
        </Section>

        <!-- Quick Reference -->
        <Section id="quick-reference" title="⚡ Quick Reference: The Six Principles">
          <p style="margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);">
            Mid game is the pivot point of the match. It's when the facade of the hero shooter
            finally falls and the MOBA comes out. No longer is the game only worried about your
            lane, but rather all three at the same time.
          </p>

          <div
            style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-md);"
          >
            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                1. Respect Lane Pressure
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Wave management is not optional. Ignoring wave is the fastest way to lose.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-purple); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                2. Protect and Punish Walkers
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                They change the entire economy. One walker = one extra item slot.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                3. Align with the 5-Minute Cycle
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Use it as your metronome. Farm minutes 10-14:30, fight at urn/bridge spawns.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-purple); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                4. Hit Your Power Spikes on Time
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Farm efficiently. Power spikes only last 2-3 minutes. Use them or lose them.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                5. Farm and Deny Efficiently
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Center sacrifices > Jungle camps. Macro soul denial snowballs advantages.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div
              style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: var(--spacing-md); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-purple);"
            >
              <div
                style="color: var(--accent-purple); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);"
              >
                6. Train Your Map Sense
              </div>
              <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
                Prediction > Reaction. Deadlock rewards the predictors, not the reactors.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div
            style="margin-top: var(--spacing-xl); text-align: center; padding: var(--spacing-lg); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 140, 66, 0.1) 0%, rgba(124, 77, 255, 0.1) 100%); border-radius: var(--border-radius-lg);"
          >
            <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0;">
              So the next time you hear those towers fall and you ask yourself,<br />
              <strong style="color: var(--accent-orange);"
                >"What the hell is Deadlock's mid game?"</strong
              >
            </p>
            <p
              style="font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--accent-purple); margin-top: var(--spacing-md); font-weight: 700;"
            >
              You'll have your answer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </Section>

        <!-- Source Attribution -->
        <Section>
          <div
            style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); padding-top: var(--spacing-lg); text-align: center;"
          >
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0;">
              Content based on <strong>"{metadata.title}"</strong> by {metadata.channel}
            </p>
            <p
              style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);"
            >
              <a
                href={metadata.videoUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                style="color: var(--accent-orange); text-decoration: none;"
              >
                🎥 Watch the full video ({metadata.duration})
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </Section>
      </Container>
    </main>

    <style>
      /* Review comment markers (only show in review status) */
      .review-comment {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-left: 4px;
        cursor: help;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
